-- Cases for the brief of this run: can the once-in-12-months limit on rent increases (ss 30(1)(b),
-- 31A(2)(b)(ii)) be avoided by ending one tenancy and starting another? How ss 30, 31A, 31B, 60, 64, 70A
-- and 76C fit together across consecutive agreements: the same parties; different tenants; a gap between
-- agreements; fixed term to periodic; periodic to fixed term; a rent fixed by a new agreement against an
-- increase by notice under s 30. Where a fork decides the answer, both readings are asserted.
-- All premises are "1 Example St" and, unless said otherwise, the lessor is "L". No public holidays are
-- supplied; weekends are computed. LQA step 4A, 4 October 2026.

IMPORT `part-1-definitions`
IMPORT `regulations-1989`
IMPORT `part-6-boundary`
IMPORT `part-3-div-3-retaliatory-action`
IMPORT `part-5-termination`
IMPORT `part-4-div-1-rent-and-bonds`
IMPORT `part-7-transitional-2024`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-extra`

§ `Fixtures`

`none` MEANS EMPTY

-- An agreement for 1 Example St with the lessor L (who granted it), no s 70A notice and no delivery of
-- possession unless given.
GIVEN nme IS A STRING
      tns IS A LIST OF STRING
      kd  IS A `Kind of tenancy`
      st  IS A NUMBER
      ex  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      wr  IS A NUMBER
      so  IS A BOOLEAN
      te  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`the agreement named` nme `with` tns `,` kd `from day` st `, expiry` ex `, at weekly rent` wr `, increases set out:` so `, terminated` te MEANS
    `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH
        `name`                                           IS nme
        `lessor`                                         IS "L"
        `granted by`                                     IS "L"
        `tenants`                                        IS tns
        `premises`                                       IS "1 Example St"
        `kind`                                           IS kd
        `rent basis`                                     IS `a fixed amount`
        `entered into on`                                IS st
        `tenancy commenced on`                           IS st
        `expiry day`                                     IS ex
        `weekly rent`                                    IS wr
        `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS so
        `provides that the rent may increase`            IS so
        `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS FALSE
        `notices under s 70A`                            IS EMPTY
        `possession delivered up on`                     IS te
        `terminated on`                                  IS te
        `status`                                         IS `no special status`

`fixed` MEANS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
`periodic` MEANS `a periodic tenancy`

GIVEN nm IS A STRING, g IS A NUMBER, e IS A NUMBER, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Rent variation`
`an increase under s 30 of` nm `noticed on day` g `, taking effect on day` e `, to` r MEANS
    `Rent variation` WITH `agreement` IS nm, `under` IS `section 30`, `notice given on` IS g, `took effect on` IS e, `weekly rent from then` IS r

GIVEN as IS A LIST OF `Residential tenancy agreement`
      vs IS A LIST OF `Rent variation`
GIVETH A `Rent history`
`the history of` as `with` vs MEANS `Rent history` WITH `agreements` IS as, `variations` IS vs

§ `A -- Fixed term renewed by a new fixed term, the same parties, no notice under s 70A`

-- A1: two years from 1 January 2025, increases set out; its rent rose under s 30 from $500 to $530 on
-- 1 January 2026 (notice 1 October 2025). A2: a new fixed term for 2027 between the same parties, at a
-- rent of $600 that the new agreement itself fixes. No notice under s 70A was given for A1.
`A1` MEANS `the agreement named` "A1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2026 12 31)) `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` TRUE `, terminated` NOTHING
`A2` MEANS `the agreement named` "A2" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2027 12 31)) `, at weekly rent` 600 `, increases set out:` TRUE `, terminated` NOTHING
`history A` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `A1`, `A2`) `with` (LIST (`an increase under s 30 of` "A1" `noticed on day` (`day number` 2025 10 1) `, taking effect on day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, to` 530))

-- s 31B(2): A2 is taken to be a continuation of A1 (FK-16 A: A1's term ended on its expiry day). On FK-16 B,
-- A1's term did not end (s 70A(2): no notice; s 76C continues it), so A2 is not a continuation.
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `A2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `A1` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`on` `FK-16 reading B` `, s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `A2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `A1` `, given the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `s 31B -- the agreements whose rent history counts for` `A2` `in` `history A` `, given the holidays` `none` EQUALS LIST "A2", "A1"
-- s 60 and s 76C: no circumstance in s 60(1) ends A1 when the parties make A2 and the tenant stays, so
-- s 76C continues A1 as a periodic tenancy from 1 January 2027 -- beside A2.
#ASSERT `s 60(1) -- the day the agreement terminates in` (`a further agreement between the same parties for the premises, the tenant staying in possession` (`day number` 2027 1 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76C(2) -- the first day of the periodic tenancy continuing` `A1` `, given the holidays` `none` EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2027 1 1)
-- FK-01: the $600 fixed by A2 is not an increase (A), so nothing in s 30 limits it; on reading B it is an
-- increase above the $530 payable under A1, made otherwise than by notice under s 30.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `A2` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history A` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `FK-01 reading B -- s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `A2` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history A` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT `the weekly rent payable under` `A1` `on day` (`day number` 2026 12 31) `, given` `history A` EQUALS 530
#ASSERT `the weekly rent payable under` `A2` `on day` (`day number` 2027 1 1) `, given` `history A` EQUALS 600
-- A notice under A2 given 1 January 2027 for $650 from 3 March 2027: the 12 months run from the last
-- increase under s 30, under A1 on 1 January 2026, so the increase is good -- 2 months after A2 raised the
-- rent to $600. Had A2 not been a continuation (FK-16 B), the 12 months would run from A2's own
-- commencement and the increase could not take effect before 1 January 2028.
`A2's notice for 3 March 2027` MEANS `a s 30 notice under` "A2" `given on day` (`day number` 2027 1 1) `for weekly rent` 650 `from day` (`day number` 2027 3 3)
#ASSERT `s 30 -- the notice` `A2's notice for 3 March 2027` `increases the rent under` `A2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history A` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`on` `under s 31B FK-16 reading B` `, s 30 -- the notice` `A2's notice for 3 March 2027` `increases the rent under` `A2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history A` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `s 30(1) -- the earliest day an increase noticed on day` (`day number` 2027 1 1) `under` `A2` `may take effect, given` `history A` `and the holidays` `none` EQUALS `day number` 2027 3 3
#ASSERT `on` `the readings taken (s 30(1)(b))` `, s 30(1)(b) -- the day the 12 months run from, for an increase on day` (`day number` 2027 3 3) `under` `A2` `, given` `history A` `and the holidays` `none` EQUALS `day number` 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `on` `under s 31B FK-16 reading B` `, s 30(1)(b) -- the day the 12 months run from, for an increase on day` (`day number` 2027 3 3) `under` `A2` `, given` `history A` `and the holidays` `none` EQUALS `day number` 2027 1 1
-- Under one agreement the same lessor could not do this: a second increase under A1 two months after the
-- first fails s 30(1)(b).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "A1" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 1 2) `for weekly rent` 600 `from day` (`day number` 2026 3 4)) `increases the rent under` `A1` `from the day it specifies, given` `history A` `and the holidays` `none`)

§ `B -- A gap between agreements`

-- B1: periodic from 1 January 2025 at $500; its rent rose under s 30 to $540 on 1 January 2026; it ended
-- on 30 June 2026 (notice and vacant possession). B2: the same parties, periodic, from 2 July 2026 at $620,
-- one clear day later. B2x: the same, but from 1 July 2026.
`B1` MEANS `the agreement named` "B1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` (JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30))
`B2` MEANS `the agreement named` "B2" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 2) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 620 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`B2x` MEANS `the agreement named` "B2x" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 620 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`B's increase` MEANS `an increase under s 30 of` "B1" `noticed on day` (`day number` 2025 10 1) `, taking effect on day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, to` 540
`history B` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `B1`, `B2`) `with` (LIST `B's increase`)
`history Bx` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `B1`, `B2x`) `with` (LIST `B's increase`)

#ASSERT NOT (`s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `B2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `B1` `, given the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `B2x` `is taken to be a continuation of` `B1` `, given the holidays` `none`
-- With the gap, the 12 months run from B2's commencement (2 July 2026); without it, from B1's increase on
-- 1 January 2026. Either way the $620 that the new agreement fixed was not limited (FK-01 A).
#ASSERT `on` `the readings taken (s 30(1)(b))` `, s 30(1)(b) -- the day the 12 months run from, for an increase on day` (`day number` 2027 1 1) `under` `B2` `, given` `history B` `and the holidays` `none` EQUALS `day number` 2026 7 2
#ASSERT `on` `the readings taken (s 30(1)(b))` `, s 30(1)(b) -- the day the 12 months run from, for an increase on day` (`day number` 2027 1 1) `under` `B2x` `, given` `history Bx` `and the holidays` `none` EQUALS `day number` 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "B2x" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 10 1) `for weekly rent` 660 `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1)) `increases the rent under` `B2x` `from the day it specifies, given` `history Bx` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "B2" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 10 1) `for weekly rent` 660 `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1)) `increases the rent under` `B2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history B` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "B2" `given on day` (`day number` 2027 4 1) `for weekly rent` 660 `from day` (`day number` 2027 7 2)) `increases the rent under` `B2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history B` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `B2x` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history Bx` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `FK-01 reading B -- s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `B2x` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history Bx` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`FK-01 reading B -- s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `B2` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history B` `and the holidays` `none`)

§ `C -- Different tenants, and a different lessor`

-- C1: periodic from 1 January 2025, tenants T1 and T2, $500; increase to $550 on 1 January 2026; ended
-- 30 June 2026. From 1 July 2026: C2 with T2 and T3 at $620; C3 with T3 alone at $700.
`C1` MEANS `the agreement named` "C1" `with` (LIST "T1", "T2") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` (JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30))
`C2` MEANS `the agreement named` "C2" `with` (LIST "T2", "T3") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 620 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`C3` MEANS `the agreement named` "C3" `with` (LIST "T3") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 700 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`C's increase` MEANS `an increase under s 30 of` "C1" `noticed on day` (`day number` 2025 10 1) `, taking effect on day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, to` 550
`history C` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `C1`, `C2`, `C3`) `with` (LIST `C's increase`)

-- s 31B(3)(b): one co-tenant in common is enough; none is not.
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `C2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `C1` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `C3` `is taken to be a continuation of` `C1` `, given the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `s 31B -- the agreements whose rent history counts for` `C3` `in` `history C` `, given the holidays` `none` EQUALS LIST "C3"
-- C2: the next increase may take effect from 1 January 2027; C3 (a new tenant, a rent set at will): not
-- before 1 July 2027. The limit attaches to the parties, not to the premises.
#ASSERT `s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "C2" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 10 1) `for weekly rent` 650 `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1)) `increases the rent under` `C2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history C` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "C2" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 10 1) `for weekly rent` 650 `from day` (`day number` 2026 12 31)) `increases the rent under` `C2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history C` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "C3" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 10 1) `for weekly rent` 730 `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1)) `increases the rent under` `C3` `from the day it specifies, given` `history C` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "C3" `given on day` (`day number` 2027 4 1) `for weekly rent` 730 `from day` (`day number` 2027 7 1)) `increases the rent under` `C3` `from the day it specifies, given` `history C` `and the holidays` `none`
-- A new lessor: C1 was sold and assigned to P, who on 1 July 2026 makes C4 with the same tenants. FK-13 A:
-- the lessor under C1 at its end is P (s 3 "lessor" includes an assignee), so C4 continues C1; FK-13 B: C1
-- was granted by L, so it does not.
`C1 assigned to P` MEANS `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH `name` IS "C1P", `lessor` IS "P", `granted by` IS "L", `tenants` IS (LIST "T1", "T2"), `premises` IS "1 Example St", `kind` IS `a periodic tenancy`, `rent basis` IS `a fixed amount`, `entered into on` IS `day number` 2025 1 1, `tenancy commenced on` IS `day number` 2025 1 1, `expiry day` IS NOTHING, `weekly rent` IS 500, `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE, `provides that the rent may increase` IS FALSE, `rent increases excluded by agreement` IS FALSE, `notices under s 70A` IS EMPTY, `possession delivered up on` IS JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30), `terminated on` IS JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30), `status` IS `no special status`
`C4` MEANS `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH `name` IS "C4", `lessor` IS "P", `granted by` IS "P", `tenants` IS (LIST "T1", "T2"), `premises` IS "1 Example St", `kind` IS `a periodic tenancy`, `rent basis` IS `a fixed amount`, `entered into on` IS `day number` 2026 7 1, `tenancy commenced on` IS `day number` 2026 7 1, `expiry day` IS NOTHING, `weekly rent` IS 640, `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE, `provides that the rent may increase` IS FALSE, `rent increases excluded by agreement` IS FALSE, `notices under s 70A` IS EMPTY, `possession delivered up on` IS NOTHING, `terminated on` IS NOTHING, `status` IS `no special status`
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `C4` `is taken to be a continuation of` `C1 assigned to P` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`on` `FK-13 reading B` `, s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `C4` `is taken to be a continuation of` `C1 assigned to P` `, given the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `C4` `is taken to be a continuation of` `C1` `, given the holidays` `none`)

§ `D -- Fixed term to periodic under s 76C`

-- D1: fixed term for 2025 at $500, increases not set out, no notice under s 70A, not terminated. It
-- continues as a periodic tenancy from 1 January 2026: the same agreement, so no s 31B question arises.
`D1` MEANS `the agreement named` "D1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2025 12 31)) `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`history D` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `D1`) `with` EMPTY
GIVEN e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Notice of increase of rent`
`D1's notice for` e MEANS `a s 30 notice under` "D1" `given on day` (`day number` 2025 10 1) `for weekly rent` 540 `from day` e

#ASSERT `s 76C(2) -- the first day of the periodic tenancy continuing` `D1` `, given the holidays` `none` EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 1 1)
-- A notice given on 1 October 2025, during the fixed term, for an increase from 1 January 2026, after it:
-- good on FK-03 A and FK-19 A; bad on FK-03 B (the notice was given during the term).
#ASSERT `s 30 -- the notice` (`D1's notice for` (`day number` 2026 1 1)) `increases the rent under` `D1` `from the day it specifies, given` `history D` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`FK-03 reading B -- s 30(2)(a) -- the right to increase is exercisable for` (`D1's notice for` (`day number` 2026 1 1)) `under` `D1` `, given the holidays` `none`)
-- An increase from 31 December 2025 would fall during the term, with nothing set out: not exercisable.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(2)(a) -- the right to increase is exercisable for` (`D1's notice for` (`day number` 2025 12 31)) `under` `D1` `, given the holidays` `none`)
-- FK-19: an increase from 1 June 2026 (notice 1 March 2026): the 12 months run from 1 January 2025, the
-- commencement of the tenancy s 76C continues (A); on B they run from 1 January 2026 and the increase fails.
`D1's March notice` MEANS `a s 30 notice under` "D1" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for weekly rent` 540 `from day` (`day number` 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `s 30 -- the notice` `D1's March notice` `increases the rent under` `D1` `from the day it specifies, given` `history D` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`on` `FK-19 reading B` `, s 30 -- the notice` `D1's March notice` `increases the rent under` `D1` `from the day it specifies, given` `history D` `and the holidays` `none`)

§ `E -- Periodic to fixed term`

-- E1: periodic from 1 January 2025 at $500, increased under s 30 to $540 on 1 January 2026. E2: a fixed
-- term from 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027 at $600, increases set out, the same parties.
-- (i) The parties agree to replace E1 and the tenant stays: no circumstance in s 60(1) ends E1, so E1 has no
-- end of term and E2 continues nothing; E1 is still in force beside E2.
`E1, still in force` MEANS `the agreement named` "E1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`E1, ended 30 June 2026 with vacant possession` MEANS `the agreement named` "E1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` (JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30))
`E2` MEANS `the agreement named` "E2" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2027 6 30)) `, at weekly rent` 600 `, increases set out:` TRUE `, terminated` NOTHING
`E's increase` MEANS `an increase under s 30 of` "E1" `noticed on day` (`day number` 2025 10 1) `, taking effect on day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, to` 540
`history E (i)` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `E1, still in force`, `E2`) `with` (LIST `E's increase`)
`history E (ii)` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `E1, ended 30 June 2026 with vacant possession`, `E2`) `with` (LIST `E's increase`)
`E2's notice` MEANS `a s 30 notice under` "E2" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 10 1) `for weekly rent` 630 `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1)

#ASSERT `s 60(1) -- the day the agreement terminates in` (`an agreement to terminate, the tenant staying in possession` (`day number` 2026 6 30)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 -- day` (`day number` 2026 8 1) `falls in the tenancy period of` `E1, still in force`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `E2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `E1, still in force` `, given the holidays` `none`)
-- (i): E2's 12 months run from its own commencement; a set-out increase from 1 January 2027 fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30 -- the notice` `E2's notice` `increases the rent under` `E2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history E (i)` `and the holidays` `none`)
-- (ii) The tenant delivered up vacant possession under a written agreement ending E1 on 30 June 2026
-- (s 60(1)(g)) and E2 began next day. FK-17 A: E1's term ended on 30 June, so E2 continues it and the 12
-- months run from E1's increase: the increase from 1 January 2027 is good. FK-17 B: a periodic tenancy has
-- no "term", so E2 continues nothing and the increase fails.
#ASSERT `s 60(1) -- the day the agreement terminates in` (`vacant possession under a written agreement to terminate (s 60(1)(g))` (`day number` 2026 6 30)) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `E2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `E1, ended 30 June 2026 with vacant possession` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT `s 30 -- the notice` `E2's notice` `increases the rent under` `E2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history E (ii)` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`on` `FK-17 reading B` `, s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `E2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `E1, ended 30 June 2026 with vacant possession` `, given the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT NOT (`on` `under s 31B FK-17 reading B` `, s 30 -- the notice` `E2's notice` `increases the rent under` `E2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history E (ii)` `and the holidays` `none`)

§ `F -- A rent fixed by each new agreement against an increase by notice`

-- F1, F2, F3: successive six-month fixed terms between the same parties at $500, $550 and $600; no notice
-- under s 70A, so each continues under s 76C beside the next. Each is a continuation of the one before.
`F1` MEANS `the agreement named` "F1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30)) `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`F2` MEANS `the agreement named` "F2" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2026 12 31)) `, at weekly rent` 550 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`F3` MEANS `the agreement named` "F3" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2027 6 30)) `, at weekly rent` 600 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`history F` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `F1`, `F2`, `F3`) `with` EMPTY

#ASSERT `s 31B -- the agreements whose rent history counts for` `F3` `in` `history F` `, given the holidays` `none` EQUALS LIST "F3", "F2", "F1"
#ASSERT `s 76C(1) -- the section applies to` `F1` `, given the holidays` `none`
-- FK-01: the rent rises every six months, by agreement: not an increase (A), so lawful; an increase
-- otherwise than under s 30 on reading B.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `F2` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history F` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `F3` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history F` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `FK-01 reading B -- s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `F2` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history F` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT `FK-01 reading B -- s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `F3` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `history F` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT `the weekly rent payable under` `F3` `on day` (`day number` 2027 1 1) `, given` `history F` EQUALS 600
-- The same rises by notice under one periodic agreement G from 1 January 2026 are not possible: an increase
-- to $550 from 1 July 2026 fails s 30(1)(b).
`G` MEANS `the agreement named` "G" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "G" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 4 1) `for weekly rent` 550 `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1)) `increases the rent under` `G` `from the day it specifies, given` (`the history of` (LIST `G`) `with` EMPTY) `and the holidays` `none`)
-- No increase under s 30 ever happened in the F chain, so the 12 months for F3 run from F3's own
-- commencement (FK-18 A), or from F1's on FK-18 B.
#ASSERT `on` `the readings taken (s 30(1)(b))` `, s 30(1)(b) -- the day the 12 months run from, for an increase on day` (`day number` 2027 6 1) `under` `F3` `, given` `history F` `and the holidays` `none` EQUALS `day number` 2027 1 1
#ASSERT `on` `FK-18 reading B` `, s 30(1)(b) -- the day the 12 months run from, for an increase on day` (`day number` 2027 6 1) `under` `F3` `, given` `history F` `and the holidays` `none` EQUALS `day number` 2026 1 1
-- s 26A and FK-11: offering F2 at a higher rent because the tenant asked for repairs is not retaliatory
-- action on reading A (not an increase "under the residential tenancy agreement", not a refusal); it is on B.
`F2 after a repair request` MEANS `Alleged retaliation` WITH `matter` IS `the tenant or a representative entity took action to enforce the tenant's rights (s 26B(2)(a))`, `the matter arose on` IS `day number` 2026 5 1, `action` IS `a higher rent under a further agreement with the tenant`, `the action was taken on` IS `day number` 2026 6 1, `the lessor was motivated, wholly or partly, by the matter arising` IS TRUE, `the tenant reasonably believes the action was retaliatory` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26A -- the lessor takes retaliatory action` `F2 after a repair request`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26B(3) -- the tenant may apply to a competent court for relief` `F2 after a repair request`)
#ASSERT `FK-11 reading B -- s 26A -- the lessor takes retaliatory action` `F2 after a repair request`
-- s 82(2): entering into F2 "with intent ... to defeat, evade or prevent the operation of this Act" is an
-- offence; whether that was the intent is a fact.
#ASSERT `s 82(2) -- entering into it is an offence` (`Term or arrangement` WITH `inconsistent with a provision of the Act` IS FALSE, `purports to exclude, modify or restrict the operation of the Act` IS FALSE, `provided for under the Act` IS FALSE, `a purported waiver of a right conferred by or under the Act` IS FALSE, `entered into with intent to defeat, evade or prevent the operation of the Act` IS TRUE) `in` `F2`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(1)(a) -- the term is void` (`Term or arrangement` WITH `inconsistent with a provision of the Act` IS FALSE, `purports to exclude, modify or restrict the operation of the Act` IS FALSE, `provided for under the Act` IS FALSE, `a purported waiver of a right conferred by or under the Act` IS FALSE, `entered into with intent to defeat, evade or prevent the operation of the Act` IS TRUE) `in` `F2`)
-- s 32(2): no notice of an increase was received, so the tenant of F2 has no trigger for an application.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32(2) -- an application on day` (`day number` 2026 7 10) `after` `no notice and no reduction` `is in time, a greater period allowed:` TRUE `, given the holidays` `none`)
-- s 31: the new agreement's higher rent is not a relevant event for increasing the bond under s 31; F2's bond
-- is limited by s 29(1)(b) at its own rent.
#ASSERT NOT (`r 5CB -- s 31(1AA) -- is a relevant event` `some other event`)
#ASSERT `s 29(1)(b) -- the most a security bond may be, at weekly rent` 550 `, a pet permitted:` FALSE EQUALS 2200

§ `G -- From s 99 to the present s 30 across a renewal`

-- G1: fixed term from 1 February 2024 to 31 January 2025, entered before the commencement, increases set
-- out: s 99 continues the former s 30 until 31 January 2025. Its rent rose to $520 on 1 August 2024 under
-- the former s 30 (6 months). G2: a new fixed term for the next year, entered 1 February 2025, at $560.
`G1` MEANS `the agreement named` "G1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2024 2 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2025 1 31)) `, at weekly rent` 500 `, increases set out:` TRUE `, terminated` NOTHING
`G2` MEANS `the agreement named` "G2" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2025 2 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2026 1 31)) `, at weekly rent` 560 `, increases set out:` TRUE `, terminated` NOTHING
`G1's notice` MEANS `Notice of increase of rent` WITH `under` IS `section 30`, `agreement` IS "G1", `given by the lessor` IS TRUE, `in writing` IS TRUE, `form` IS `a form approved by the Minister`, `specifies the increased rent or the change` IS TRUE, `specifies the day` IS TRUE, `given` IS `handed over on day` (`day number` 2024 5 1), `takes effect on` IS `day number` 2024 8 1, `weekly rent from then` IS 520, `withdrawn` IS FALSE, `within any limit agreed under s 30(2)(b)` IS TRUE, `any departure from the required form is immaterial and not misleading` IS TRUE
`G's increase` MEANS `Rent variation` WITH `agreement` IS "G1", `under` IS `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024`, `notice given on` IS `day number` 2024 5 1, `took effect on` IS `day number` 2024 8 1, `weekly rent from then` IS 520
`history G before` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `G1`) `with` EMPTY
`history G` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `G1`, `G2`) `with` (LIST `G's increase`)
`G2's notice` MEANS `a s 30 notice under` "G2" `given on day` (`day number` 2025 5 1) `for weekly rent` 580 `from day` (`day number` 2025 8 1)

#ASSERT `s 99(2) -- the section applies to` `G1` `, given` (`the facts for ss 99 and 100 of` `G1`)
#ASSERT `the notice` `G1's notice` `has effect under` `G1` `, given` `history G before` `,` (`the facts for ss 99 and 100 of` `G1`) `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `G2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `G1` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 99(2) -- the section applies to` `G2` `, given` (`the facts for ss 99 and 100 of` `G2`))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 100(2) -- the section applies to` `G2` `, given` (`the facts for ss 99 and 100 of` `G2`))
-- G2's increase from 1 August 2025: 12 months after G1's increase under the former s 30 (FK-04 A): good.
-- On FK-04 B that increase does not count, the 12 months run from G2's commencement, and it fails.
#ASSERT `the notice` `G2's notice` `has effect under` `G2` `, given` `history G` `,` (`the facts for ss 99 and 100 of` `G2`) `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`on` `FK-04 reading B` `, s 30 -- the notice` `G2's notice` `increases the rent under` `G2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history G` `and the holidays` `none`)
-- An increase under G2 from 1 July 2025 fails (12 months from 1 August 2024).
#ASSERT NOT (`the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "G2" `given on day` (`day number` 2025 4 1) `for weekly rent` 580 `from day` (`day number` 2025 7 1)) `has effect under` `G2` `, given` `history G` `,` (`the facts for ss 99 and 100 of` `G2`) `and the holidays` `none`)

§ `H -- An order under s 32 and a new agreement (FK-23)`

-- H1: periodic from 1 January 2026 at $600. On 1 March 2026 a court orders under s 32(4) that the rent not
-- exceed $500, for a period to 31 August 2026. H1 ends on 30 April 2026 (vacant possession under a written
-- agreement) and H2, between the same parties, begins on 1 May 2026 at $650.
`H1` MEANS `the agreement named` "H1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 600 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` (JUST (`day number` 2026 4 30))
`H2` MEANS `the agreement named` "H2" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `periodic` `from day` (`day number` 2026 5 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 650 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `H2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `H1` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT `s 32(5) -- an order made on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for a period ending on day` (`day number` 2026 8 31) `in respect of` `H1` `is in force on day` (`day number` 2026 4 15)
-- FK-23 A: the applicant's tenancy under H1 expired on 30 April, so on 15 May the order has no effect and
-- $650 may be demanded; FK-23 B: the applicant still occupies, the order is in force, and demanding $650 is
-- an offence under s 32(7).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32(5) -- an order made on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for a period ending on day` (`day number` 2026 8 31) `in respect of` `H1` `is in force on day` (`day number` 2026 5 15))
#ASSERT `FK-23 reading B -- s 32(5) -- an order made on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for a period ending on day` (`day number` 2026 8 31) `, the applicant still occupying:` TRUE `, is in force on day` (`day number` 2026 5 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32(7) -- demanding or receiving weekly rent of` 650 `is an offence, the order fixing` 500 `and being in force:` (`s 32(5) -- an order made on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for a period ending on day` (`day number` 2026 8 31) `in respect of` `H1` `is in force on day` (`day number` 2026 5 15)))
#ASSERT `s 32(7) -- demanding or receiving weekly rent of` 650 `is an offence, the order fixing` 500 `and being in force:` (`FK-23 reading B -- s 32(5) -- an order made on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for a period ending on day` (`day number` 2026 8 31) `, the applicant still occupying:` TRUE `, is in force on day` (`day number` 2026 5 15))
-- And while the order was in force under H1, a s 64 notice to end H1 would have been ineffectual (s 65(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `s 65(1)(a) -- a notice of termination under s 64 is ineffectual` (`Section 32 status` WITH `proceedings are pending for an order under s 32 fixing the maximum rent` IS FALSE, `an order under s 32 fixing the maximum rent is in force` IS `s 32(5) -- an order made on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for a period ending on day` (`day number` 2026 8 31) `in respect of` `H1` `is in force on day` (`day number` 2026 4 15))

§ `I -- Ending a periodic tenancy without grounds after a repair request`

-- The tenant of a periodic tenancy asks for repairs on 1 March 2026; on 10 March the lessor gives a notice
-- under s 64 for possession on 15 May 2026, motivated by the request, meaning to let the premises again at
-- a higher rent. The notice is a notice under s 64 (60 clear days); it is retaliatory action (s 26A(a)(iii));
-- s 26B applies and the tenant may apply to a court, as the note to s 64(3) points out.
`I's s 64 notice` MEANS `Notice under s 64` WITH `given on` IS `day number` 2026 3 10, `received by the tenant on` IS `day number` 2026 3 10, `possession day specified` IS `day number` 2026 5 15
`I's retaliation` MEANS `Alleged retaliation` WITH `matter` IS `the tenant or a representative entity took action to enforce the tenant's rights (s 26B(2)(a))`, `the matter arose on` IS `day number` 2026 3 1, `action` IS `action to terminate the agreement`, `the action was taken on` IS `day number` 2026 3 10, `the lessor was motivated, wholly or partly, by the matter arising` IS TRUE, `the tenant reasonably believes the action was retaliatory` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64 -- the notice` `I's s 64 notice` `is a notice of termination under the section for` `G` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT `s 26A -- the lessor takes retaliatory action` `I's retaliation`
#ASSERT `s 64(3), note -- the tenant given a s 64 notice may also apply under s 26B` `I's retaliation`
#ASSERT `s 26B(4) -- the court may make, on the application` `I's retaliation` `, satisfied:` TRUE `, the order` `an order setting aside the lessor's action`

§ `J -- Income-based rent across agreements (ss 31A and 31B(1)(b))`

-- J1: periodic from 1 January 2025, rent calculated by reference to the tenant's income; the method was
-- changed under s 31A from 1 January 2026; J1 ended on 30 June 2026. J2 (the same parties) begins on 1 July
-- 2026; J3 (the same parties) begins on 3 July 2026, after a gap.
GIVEN nme IS A STRING, st IS A NUMBER, te IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`the income-based agreement named` nme `from day` st `, terminated` te MEANS
    `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH
        `name`                                           IS nme
        `lessor`                                         IS "L"
        `granted by`                                     IS "L"
        `tenants`                                        IS LIST "T1"
        `premises`                                       IS "1 Example St"
        `kind`                                           IS `a periodic tenancy`
        `rent basis`                                     IS `calculated by reference to the tenant's income`
        `entered into on`                                IS st
        `tenancy commenced on`                           IS st
        `expiry day`                                     IS NOTHING
        `weekly rent`                                    IS 300
        `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE
        `provides that the rent may increase`            IS FALSE
        `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS FALSE
        `notices under s 70A`                            IS EMPTY
        `possession delivered up on`                     IS te
        `terminated on`                                  IS te
        `status`                                         IS `no special status`

GIVEN nm IS A STRING, g IS A NUMBER, e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Notice of increase of rent`
`a change of method under` nm `given on day` g `from day` e MEANS
    `Notice of increase of rent` WITH
        `under`                                      IS `section 31A`
        `agreement`                                  IS nm
        `given by the lessor`                        IS TRUE
        `in writing`                                 IS TRUE
        `form`                                       IS `the approved form (s 88C)`
        `specifies the increased rent or the change` IS TRUE
        `specifies the day`                          IS TRUE
        `given`                                      IS `handed over on day` g
        `takes effect on`                            IS e
        `weekly rent from then`                      IS 320
        `withdrawn`                                  IS FALSE
        `within any limit agreed under s 30(2)(b)`   IS TRUE
        `any departure from the required form is immaterial and not misleading` IS TRUE

`J1` MEANS `the income-based agreement named` "J1" `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, terminated` (JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30))
`J2` MEANS `the income-based agreement named` "J2" `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, terminated` NOTHING
`J3` MEANS `the income-based agreement named` "J3" `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 3) `, terminated` NOTHING
`J1's change` MEANS `Rent variation` WITH `agreement` IS "J1", `under` IS `section 31A`, `notice given on` IS `day number` 2025 10 1, `took effect on` IS `day number` 2026 1 1, `weekly rent from then` IS 310
`history J` MEANS `the history of` (LIST `J1`, `J2`, `J3`) `with` (LIST `J1's change`)

#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `J2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `J1` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `J3` `is taken to be a continuation of` `J1` `, given the holidays` `none`)
-- J2: the 12 months run from the change under J1 (s 31B(1)(b)): a change from 1 October 2026 fails, one from
-- 1 January 2027 is good. J3: they run from J3's own commencement, so 1 January 2027 fails and 3 July 2027 is good.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31A -- the notice` (`a change of method under` "J2" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `from day` (`day number` 2026 10 1)) `changes the method under` `J2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history J` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `s 31A -- the notice` (`a change of method under` "J2" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1)) `changes the method under` `J2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history J` `and the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31A -- the notice` (`a change of method under` "J3" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 7 3) `from day` (`day number` 2027 1 1)) `changes the method under` `J3` `from the day it specifies, given` `history J` `and the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `s 31A -- the notice` (`a change of method under` "J3" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 7 3) `from day` (`day number` 2027 7 3)) `changes the method under` `J3` `from the day it specifies, given` `history J` `and the holidays` `none`
-- A notice under s 30 is no way round s 31A: s 30(1) does not apply where the rent is income-based.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "J2" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `for weekly rent` 330 `from day` (`day number` 2026 10 1)) `increases the rent under` `J2` `from the day it specifies, given` `history J` `and the holidays` `none`)

§ `K -- A notice under s 70A that moves the end of the term (s 70A(5)), and s 31B`

-- K1: a fixed term for 2025 at $500; on 1 November 2025 the lessor gives a notice under s 70A for possession
-- on 31 January 2026, later than the expiry day, so the term expires on 31 January 2026 (s 70A(5)(a); FK-10
-- A). A new agreement between the same parties from 1 February 2026 continues K1; one from 1 January 2026
-- does not (the term had not ended). On FK-10 B the fixed term would have ended on 31 December 2025.
`K1` MEANS `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH `name` IS "K1", `lessor` IS "L", `granted by` IS "L", `tenants` IS (LIST "T1"), `premises` IS "1 Example St", `kind` IS `a tenancy for a fixed term`, `rent basis` IS `a fixed amount`, `entered into on` IS `day number` 2025 1 1, `tenancy commenced on` IS `day number` 2025 1 1, `expiry day` IS JUST (`day number` 2025 12 31), `weekly rent` IS 500, `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE, `provides that the rent may increase` IS FALSE, `rent increases excluded by agreement` IS FALSE, `notices under s 70A` IS (LIST (`Notice under s 70A` WITH `given by` IS `the lessor`, `given on` IS `day number` 2025 11 1, `possession day specified` IS `day number` 2026 1 31)), `possession delivered up on` IS NOTHING, `terminated on` IS NOTHING, `status` IS `no special status`
`K2 from 1 February 2026` MEANS `the agreement named` "K2" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2026 2 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2027 1 31)) `, at weekly rent` 580 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
`K2 from 1 January 2026` MEANS `the agreement named` "K2x" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `fixed` `from day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2026 12 31)) `, at weekly rent` 580 `, increases set out:` FALSE `, terminated` NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 70A -- the day the term of` `K1` `ends under the section, given the holidays` `none` EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `K2 from 1 February 2026` `is taken to be a continuation of` `K1` `, given the holidays` `none`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `K2 from 1 January 2026` `is taken to be a continuation of` `K1` `, given the holidays` `none`)
#ASSERT `FK-10 reading B -- the last day of the fixed term of` `K1` EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2025 12 31)
-- While the term runs to 31 January 2026 the lessor cannot give a notice under s 64 (s 64(5); FK-10 A).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64 -- the notice` (`Notice under s 64` WITH `given on` IS `day number` 2026 1 10, `received by the tenant on` IS `day number` 2026 1 10, `possession day specified` IS `day number` 2026 3 20) `is a notice of termination under the section for` `K1` `, given the holidays` `none`)
